; The doors. Each hinges on the face's -X edge, which the root's Rz(+90) turns into
; the BOTTOM edge of the machine's left side, so both drop open downward.
;
; Three nodes apiece for the same reason the SD door needs them: VRHinge writes
; target.rotation.x and Euler rotation composes in the PARENT's frame, so the basis
; has to sit on a static MOUNT and the pivot it drives has to stay at identity.
;
; Mount basis x (0,0,1), y (1,0,0), z (0,1,0) — local X along the hinge line, so
; +theta walks the free edge from the machine's +X round toward +Y and out of the
; face. Written as matrix ROWS, so the nine numbers read as the transpose.
[node name="CtrlFlapMount" type="Node3D" parent="Top"]
transform = Transform3D(0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, -0.018, 0.157, 0.0322)

[node name="CtrlFlapPivot" type="Node3D" parent="Top/CtrlFlapMount"]

[node name="Door" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="Top/CtrlFlapMount/CtrlFlapPivot"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.018, 0.0009)
mesh = SubResource("Mesh_ctrl_flap")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("Mat_offwhite")

[node name="MemFlapMount" type="Node3D" parent="Top"]
